# AI-signals pipeline working files live in data/, never in public/ — Vite copies
# public/ into dist, so anything there is published on the live site.
# These are per-run artifacts, regenerated each run.
# Globs, not exact paths: sector runs suffix the filename with the work dimension
# (data/_finder-rejected-worker-experience-identity-and-wellbeing.json), and this
# repo is public — the rejected list names stories the editorial team declined.
# (data/_seen-ledger.jsonl is committed state and is intentionally NOT ignored.)
data/_candidates*.json
data/_finder-output*.json
data/_finder-rejected*
data/_finder-report*.md

# Staged signal drafts awaiting review, and the accepted/ and rejected/ folders
# the reviewer moves them into. Local scratch: this repo is public, and a draft
# is by definition unreviewed. Only what `signals:promote` moves into
# public/content/ai-signals/ is ever committed.
data/signal-drafts/

# Brainstorming mockups (visual companion scratch space) and the implementation-ledger directory
.superpowers/

# Left behind by browser automation tooling (Playwright MCP)
.playwright-mcp/

# Claude Code session state. Note .claude/worktrees/ holds *git worktrees* —
# full checkouts of this repo. Without this rule `git add -A` commits them as
# embedded git repositories, and ESLint lints them as if they were source,
# which reports every finding several times over.
.claude/

# Vite
dist-ssr
*.local
settings.local.json
settings.json
.vscode/settings.json
FuturesofSoftwareWork.code-workspace
